_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🔴 Critical_

**Port flag will not parse correctly as a single argument.**

Line 203 pushes `-p ${availablePort}` as a single string (e.g., `"-p 6007"`). When `executeCommand` spawns the subprocess, each array element becomes one argument. The CLI will receive `"-p 6007"` as a single token rather than `-p` followed by `6007`, causing the port flag to be ignored or misinterpreted.

<details>
<summary>🐛 Proposed fix: push port flag as separate arguments</summary>

```diff
       if (useAlternativePort) {
-        parts.push(`-p ${availablePort}`);
+        parts.push('-p', String(availablePort));

         if (supportsOnboarding && shouldOnboard) {
           parts.push('--initial-path=/onboarding');
         }

         parts.push('--quiet');
       }
```
</details>

<!-- suggestion_start -->

<details>
<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>

> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**
> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.

```suggestion
      const defaultPort = 6006;
      const availablePort = await getServerPort(defaultPort);
      const useAlternativePort = availablePort !== defaultPort;

      if (useAlternativePort) {
        parts.push('-p', String(availablePort));

        if (supportsOnboarding && shouldOnboard) {
          parts.push('--initial-path=/onboarding');
        }

        parts.push('--quiet');
      }
```

</details>

<!-- suggestion_end -->

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
In `@code/lib/create-storybook/src/initiate.ts` around lines 198 - 210, The port
flag is being added as a single string token (parts.push(`-p ${availablePort}`))
which will be passed as one argument to the spawned process; change the logic
that builds the parts array so the port flag and its value are pushed as two
separate arguments (e.g., push the flag token and the port value separately)
where availablePort is used, ensuring the spawned CLI receives '-p' and the port
number as distinct arguments; keep the existing conditions around
supportsOnboarding and shouldOnboard and leave other pushes (like
'--initial-path=/onboarding' and '--quiet') unchanged.
```

</details>

